core=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation, authority changes, stale-work handling and their persistence/membership/application connections have been traced. Local read-response correlation and deeper fault variants remain questions, not unexplained core ownership.',formation=path('Peer routes proposals to leader. Leader assigns term/index, appends, and sends predecessor-qualified replication; followers match predecessor and protect committed history. Acknowledgements update per-peer matches; majority of full voters and witnesses selects an index whose term must equal current leader term. Commit is propagated via replication and bounded heartbeat commit. Engine persists state and entries before acknowledgement messages, and queues committed entries according to FastApply durability overlap. RSM applies entries and membership, then node callbacks report proposal/read completion. Rejection responses retry earlier suffix; compaction selects snapshot for active peers.', ['B-replicate','B-persist','B-apply','B-recovery'],['F-committed'],['M-core-commit','M-core-dispatch','M-log-rules','M-engine-order','M-node-consume','M-rsm-apply','M-replicate-send']),context=path('Election timers initiate campaign only for eligible full voters without committed-but-unapplied work. New term resets transient votes/progress/read confirmations; vote granting checks log freshness and prior vote, and candidate forms authority from deduplicated quorum replies. Higher-term protocol messages normally cause stepdown, with check-quorum vote suppression exception; lower terms are ignored. Same-term leader messages demote candidates. Quorum checks, removal and transfer govern loss/change of leadership. Transfer waits for target catchup and triggers target election via TimeoutNow, while blocking proposals until completion or timeout.', ['B-authority','B-membership'],[],['M-core-commit','M-core-dispatch','M-response-routing','M-timers','M-transfer','M-quorum-check','M-candidate-stepdown']),connection=path('Terms qualify newly counted support, but established committed history survives authority reset and constrains future logs and votes. Membership becomes active through RSM application; campaign defers when applied state lags commit, so a new leader does not simply form using its old unapplied membership. New leader reconstructs pending config status and commits a current-term no-op before multi-voter ReadIndex admission. Pending read contexts are reset with authority; within one leader context, voter heartbeat confirmation releases queue prefixes for local readiness or forwarded replies, and clients require exact context plus applied index. Old network responses are term-filtered and unknown responders rejected; pending client work may independently drop or timeout.', ['B-authority','B-membership','B-read-confirm','B-read-route','B-client-read','B-recovery'],['F-committed','F-read-release'],['M-core-commit','M-core-dispatch','M-peer','M-heartbeat-producer','M-read-reply','M-read-client','M-node-callbacks']),open_details=['Forwarded replies use triggering confirmation context for every released queue status; exact correlation under overlapping reads remains unresolved.', 'Disk/concurrent state machine crash/recovery, storage implementations, session deduplication and membership-change message interleavings remain deeper variants.'],core_gaps=[])
